For a long time, I was pretty sure I was having insurmountable
difficulty with the basic concepts of this game.  I've played hundreds
of games and never really made it any further than the 5th dungeon
level with a few levels of exp.  I wasn't exactly sure why I kept
playing, since I seemed to just die stupid deaths each and every time.

This time, however, something just worked right.  I was a knight (the
first time I can recall playing one in years), I managed to make my
pony (and, later, my first warhorse) loot every item from a shop.  I
managed to correctly identify which items weren't cursed, found some
decent armor, got a few good rings, etc.

So my level 6 knight and warhorse are steadily and carefully working
our way down the mines, which seem unusually un-lit to me, but
relatively easy nevertheless.  We end up on a lit level with
nightwatchmen, and for the first time I get to watch my pet kill one.
Very cool.  The next thing I know, though, some random gnome escapes a
fight by digging a hole.

As I recall, I was confused (or something... my movement wasn't working
right) so I just sort of hung out in the spot next to the hole for a
few turns, resting.  I didn't want to accidentally walk into the pit,
after all. Soon enough, another watchman walks by, right on to the spot
where the hole was dug.  I think, "well, if he didn't fall into the
hole, neither will I", so I walk onto the same square as the watchman.

The next thing I know, I'm in Gnomish Mines Level 10.  I'm pretty sure
this is very, very far from where I was.  Certainly the furthest into a
dungeon I've ever been in nethack.  Some hard gnomes and gnome lords
surround me, but I manage to fight them off and get to a relatively
secluded spot (the dungeon is unlit, and I guess I forgot I had a lamp,
because I just sort of stumbled around).  I'm in the secluded spot,
resting up, when a master mind flayer suddenly appears next to me.  I
don't exactly understand what happened, but the next thing I know, he's
taken away most of my health, my inteligence went down, and the game is
telling me that I'm pretty much screwed.  I pull an unidentified wand
out of my bag, which seems to be the only chance I've got, and zap it
in his direction.  DYWYPI?

Questions:
1) I had earlier identified a wand a speed monster.  I have no idea
what this does.  My best guess was that it would speed up an enemy
monster, which seemed like a crazy idea to me.
2) If I had chosen to pray instead of use the wand, could things have
turned out any better?


